  "kind": "recipe",
  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "standard",
    "description": "Xiaomi MiMo-V2.6-Flash-RL (309B total, 15B active, fp8 attention with MXFP4 routed experts, MIT) on two Sparks with SGLang tensor and expert parallel 2, FP8 KV, the packed-MXFP4 FlashInfer MoE path, up to 1M context and text, image, video and audio input. Basis: MiaAI-Lab's two-Spark kit (AGPL-3.0, its boot.py and engine hot-fix patch vendored unchanged, on the lmsysorg/sglang nightly-dev-cu13-20260921 image). Speculative decoding is the checkpoint's EAGLE MTP head by default (upstream default: 35.0 tok/s prose, 46.0 code, KV pool about 2.4-2.9M tokens, decode CUDA graphs off); the bundled DFlash drafter is an option (69.8 tok/s code, 25.8 prose, smaller pool). Alternatives from other creators: tonyd2wild's vLLM recipe (MIT) and r0b0tlab's NVFP4 SGLang kit. Upstream throughput figures are single-stream claims measured by upstream with sparkDash, not measured here; Vonk physical two-Spark acceptance is pending.",
    "tags": [
      "audio",
      "dflash",
      "eagle",
      "mimo-v2.6",
      "multimodal",
      "mxfp4",
      "reasoning",
      "sglang",
      "spark",
      "speculative-decoding",
      "tool-use",
      "video"
    ],
    "title": "MiMo V2.6 Flash RL SGLang two Sparks (Mia)"
  },
